            <ArticleTitle>[Effects of hydrokinezytherapy of obesity in elder women].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>16-18</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">The aim of the study was to determine the effects of regular hydrokinezytherapy on the prevention of obesity in elderly women.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIALS AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The study was carried out among the Third Age University students, participating in hydrokinezytherapy classes. The group consisted of 31 women aged 63-70 years. Body Mass Index (BMI) was calculated. The values obtained were compared with the average for the population using the assessment criteria for adults according to Ostrowska-Nawarycz. To identify the obesity type waist hip ratio (WHR) was used. The results were subjected to statistical analysis. The T-Student test was carried out.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The results of the study showed that after a year of training the number of women with the correct, while there was no change in the WHR values before and after the training.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The results of the research and literature data indicate that regular physical activity effectively prevents weight gain, reduces overweight and obesity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
